  "id": "e01q42",
  "exam": 1,
  "num": 42,
  "week": "W1",
  "explanation": "<p><strong>Answer: $\\mathbf{19}$</strong></p><p>Run the recurrence from Q31 with $R_0 = 1$, $J_0 = 1$:</p><p>8pt</p><table class='xt'><tr><th>@l c c c@ <strong>layer</strong></th><th>$K_{\\text{eff}}$</th><th>$R$</th><th>$J$ after</th></tr><tr><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>$R_0 = 1$</td><td>$J_0 = 1$</td></tr><tr><td>L1 ($K{=}5,S{=}1,D{=}1$)</td><td>$5$</td><td>$1 + 4\\cdot 1 = 5$</td><td>$1$</td></tr><tr><td>L2 ($K{=}3,S{=}2,D{=}1$)</td><td>$3$</td><td>$5 + 2\\cdot 1 = 7$</td><td>$2$</td></tr><tr><td>L3 ($K{=}3,S{=}1,D{=}3$)</td><td>$3(3{-}1){+}1 = 7$</td><td>$7 + 6\\cdot 2 = \\mathbf{19}$</td><td>$2$</td></tr></table><p><strong>Check it by hand, because trusting the recurrence blindly is how the mistake survives.</strong> Number the input $0,1,2,\\dots$ One L3 output reads three L2 units spaced $D = 3$ apart: L2 units $0, 3, 6$. Each L2 unit $u$ reads L1 units $2u, 2u{+}1, 2u{+}2$ (stride 2, $K = 3$), giving $\\{0,1,2\\}$, $\\{6,7,8\\}$, $\\{12,13,14\\}$. Each L1 unit $v$ reads inputs $v \\dots v{+}4$. Lowest input touched: $0$. Highest: $14 + 4 = 18$. So the field spans inputs $0$ through $18$ — $\\mathbf{19}$ positions.</p><p><strong>Three ways to get it wrong.</strong> Using $J_l$ instead of $J_{l-1}$ in the update; forgetting that dilation inflates $K$ before it enters the formula; and letting padding into the calculation, which never belongs there.</p>",
  "type": "numeric",
