  "exam": 1,
  "num": 43,
  "week": "W2",
  "explanation": "<p><strong>Answer: $d_k = \\mathbf{64}$; $W^{O}$ has $\\mathbf{262{,}144}$ parameters</strong></p><p>$d_k = d_{\\text{model}}/h = 512/8 = 64$. The heads partition the width rather than adding to it, which is why multi-head attention costs essentially the same as single-head over the full 512 — every term in the FLOP count contains $h$ only through $h \\cdot d_k$ or $h \\cdot d_v$, both equal to $d_{\\text{model}}$, so $h$ cancels.</p><p>$W^{O} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{h d_v \\times d_{\\text{model}}} = \\mathbb{R}^{512 \\times 512}$, so $512^2 = \\mathbf{262{,}144}$ parameters. <strong>Its job is to mix the concatenated heads</strong>, which are otherwise independent — without it, the head outputs would simply sit side by side in the vector and never interact.</p>",
