  "num": 1,
  "week": "W1",
  "explanation": "<p>Compose two affine maps and you get another one: $W_2(W_1x + b_1) + b_2 = (W_2W_1)x + (W_2b_1 + b_2)$. The product $W_2W_1$ is just some matrix, so a hundred layers express exactly what one layer expresses.</p><p><strong>1st and 3rd are the same false claim twice.</strong> Depth without non-linearity buys no expressive power, so a linear stack cannot solve XOR any more than a single perceptron can.</p><p><strong>4th true, and it is the trap.</strong> The parameter count really does grow — you are paying for depth and getting nothing. That is the sharpest way to see why the non-linearity is not a refinement but the thing that makes depth mean anything.</p>",
