  "explanation": "<p><strong>Answer: $\\mathbf{112 \\times 112 \\times 64}$; $\\mathbf{9{,}472}$ parameters</strong></p><p><strong>Output size</strong>, per spatial axis: \\[ 224 + 23 - 72 + 1 = 2232 + 1 = 111 + 1 = 112, <span>so </span> 112 112 64. \\] <strong>Parameters</strong>: $7 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 64 = 9\\,408$ weights, plus one bias per output channel, $= \\mathbf{9\\,472}$.</p><p><strong>The reason padding $3$ appears with kernel $7$.</strong> $P = (K-1)/2$ is the padding that makes a stride-$1$ convolution preserve the spatial size; with stride $2$ it makes the output exactly half. That is why the first layer of a ResNet is written $7\\times7$, stride $2$, pad $3$ — the numbers are chosen together.</p>",
