  "explanation": "<p><strong>Answer: $d_k = \\mathbf{64}$; attention $\\mathbf{2{,}359{,}296}$; feed-forward $\\mathbf{4{,}718{,}592}$</strong></p><p>$d_k = d_v = 768/12 = \\mathbf{64}$.</p><p><strong>Attention.</strong> Four projections $W^Q, W^K, W^V, W^O$, each $768 \\times 768$: $4 \\cdot 768^2 = \\mathbf{2\\,359\\,296}$.</p><p><strong>Feed-forward.</strong> Up to $4d = 3072$ and back: $2 \\cdot 768 \\cdot 3072 = \\mathbf{4\\,718\\,592}$.</p><p><strong>Two things worth taking from these numbers.</strong> First, $h$ does not appear anywhere: the projections are $d \\times d$ whether you split them into $12$ heads or none, which is the arithmetic behind Q10. Second, <strong>the feed-forward network is twice the size of the attention</strong> — about two thirds of a transformer layer's parameters sit in the part that does no mixing at all. It is the attention that gets the attention, and the FFN that gets the parameters.</p>",
